① $n=1,2m+n-1=42$, solving get $m=20.5$, not an integer, ignore it;  
② $n=2,2m+n-1=21$, solving get $m=9$, it is an integer;  
③ $n=3,2m+n-1=14$, solving get $m=4$, it is an integer;  
④ $n=6,2m+n-1=7$, solving get $m=1$, it is an integer. Since 6 is the largest value for $n$ among these four, the largest number of positive, consecutive integers whose sum is 21 is 6.</think> <answer> 6 </answer>

